  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run `vite build` or view a render, so the look is untested in a browser. The shader's transparency and the glow are the parts most likely to need adjusting.\n\n- **Shield:** a sphere with a custom GLSL material. It has a cyan fresnel rim, sine scanlines that scroll upward through world-space y, and a faint sweeping band. The material is transparent with alpha-blending and depth write off. A `clk` uniform is pushed every frame with `setUniform`, because `uTime` doesn't advance on this version.\n- **Cube:** a small metallic PBR cube sits inside the sphere and rotates on all three axes. The neutral environment and a directional light give the metal something to reflect.\n- **Scene:** the background is dark (`#04070d`). The floor is a dark, glossy, partly metallic plane. A cyan point light under the sphere and a bloom effect put the glow on the floor. The perspective camera frames the sphere.\n- **Ready flag:** it sets `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true` two animation frames after `app.ready()` resolves. `createAuraApp` drives the render loop.\n\n",
